# FRONTIER POD RUN env (2026-09-07; Plan_2026-09-07_Instrument_Suite §4 / Plan_2026-09-07_Frontier_Registration.md) — "the
# comparator rows at the full protocol": the public TRM-class Sudoku checkpoints (alphaXiv TRM-MLP + its 60k grid, CGAR, EqR)
# ported into our checkpoint format and read through OUR evaluator on ONE v6e-8 at Night A's exact protocol, plus PASS TWO of
# Night A (the DEC wide arms' 5k x k32 scans A3 A7 A5 A4 A8 under the scan-deadlock canary, and the DEC D128 rows). EVAL-ONLY:
# every job idempotent by its GCS marker; the live 5-min bank keeps the evaluators' 300 s partials across preemptions; a relaunch
# resumes at the first missing marker. Walls (measured on Night A's 8): ~106 min per model x 3 + EqR extras 33 + trmpub60k 11 +
# DEC scans ~17 min x 5 + D128 rows 12 -> ~8.5 h + compile/markers -> cap launch + 18 h. US-first (standing policy); Mumbai last.
# The previous (Night A) env is preserved in git (commit bba59cd and earlier).
POD=qhrrn2-pod2
ZONES="us-east1-d us-east5-b us-central1-a us-central2-b us-west1-c asia-south1-c"
ACCEL=v6e-8
ACCEL_LIST="v6e-8"
BIG_MAX_STRIKES=2
R_TAG=frontier
R_D=384
R_STEPS=0
ARMS=""
CHAIN_SCRIPT=tools/chain_frontier.sh
CHAIN_EXTRA_ENV="SELF_TEARDOWN=1"
WALL=61200
SENTINEL=CHAIN-FRONTIER-COMPLETE
GCS=gs://qhrrn2-rescue/frontier
FINAL_OBJ=frontier_final.tgz
CANARY_CKPT=runs/pretrain6_d24/ckpt_latest.pkl
